<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gerard of Roussillon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died c. 878</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Girart de Roussillon, Girart of Vienne, Gerard II of Paris</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gerard of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roussillon">Roussillon</a> was a Frankish count, a supporter of the emperor Lothar I, who governed the kingdom of Provence for the young king Charles of Provence from 855. As count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienne">Vienne</a> he defended the kingdom against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bald">Charles the Bald</a> and fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Vikings</a> who raided up the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhone">Rhône</a> around 860. Charles the Bald took Vienne in 870. He became the hero of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-french">Old French</a> epic Girart de Roussillon.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gerard-of-roussillon.jpg" alt="Gerard of Roussillon" width="320" height="233" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anonymous miniaturist, Netherlandish · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Girart_de_Roussillon.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
